  "question": "What is the federal simplified acquisition threshold?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The federal simplified acquisition threshold is $350,000. This rule is defined in the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) 2.101. The threshold can be higher, such as $1 million for certain contingency operations or emergency responses.",
